description:
Retrieve a device

Returns a device with its model, serial number, site, last contact and battery level.

GET /v2/devices/{device_id}

Update a device

Updates the name, the site or the reporting interval of a device. Only the fields given are changed.

PATCH /v2/devices/{device_id}

Delete a device

Deletes a device and its configuration. Its past readings are kept.

DELETE /v2/devices/{device_id}

Retrieve a gateway

Returns a gateway with its connection state, signal strength and the devices it relays.

GET /v2/gateways/{gateway_id}

Delete a gateway

Deletes a gateway. The devices it relayed stay registered but stop reporting until another gateway reaches them.

DELETE /v2/gateways/{gateway_id}

Update a site

Updates the name, the address or the time zone of a site.

PATCH /v2/sites/{site_id}

Delete a site

Deletes a site. It must hold no device and no gateway.

DELETE /v2/sites/{site_id}

Delete an alert

Deletes an alert from the history.

DELETE /v2/alerts/{alert_id}

Update an alert rule

Updates the threshold, the duration or the recipients of an alert rule, or pauses it.

PATCH /v2/alert-rules/{rule_id}

Delete an alert rule

Deletes an alert rule. The alerts it raised are kept.

DELETE /v2/alert-rules/{rule_id}

Update a user

Changes the role of a user.

PATCH /v2/users/{user_id}

Remove a user

Removes a user from the organization. Their API keys are revoked.

DELETE /v2/users/{user_id}

Revoke an API key

Revokes an API key at once. Calls made with it are refused from then on.

DELETE /v2/api-keys/{key_id}

Delete a webhook

Deletes a webhook. No more events are sent to its URL.

DELETE /v2/webhooks/{webhook_id}

Retrieve an export

Returns the state of an export and, once it is ready, the link to download the file.

GET /v2/exports/{export_id}
